KG42.register("clusters-c0ee9bfcec2b125e53ca3511",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v142-d-K002","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","label":"STEP two-stage joint trading, scenario fulfillment, and community net-cost allocation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"STEP two-stage joint trading, scenario fulfillment, and community net-cost allocation","market_meaning":"STEP coordinates day-ahead bids and resource allocation according to community rules and demand and generation forecasts, arranges remedial trading and energy storage use under renewable generation and intraday price scenarios, maintains household-by-household supply-demand security, and fulfills day-ahead commitments already made. The external electricity purchase cost and the day-ahead feed-in compensation together constitute the community's expected net-cost objective; trading permissions and source conditions must apply separately according to the comparison scenario.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM","LEM_DEM"],"process_stages":["participation","coordination","bidding","clearing","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The chains all belong to one two-stage community framework, and coordination, allocation, trading, and cost accounting share a common decision object. The resource and trading conditions of Base, BAT, P2P, and STEP must be kept separate; the trigger conventions distinguishing optional bids from obligatory commitments, the interface between aggregate P2P quantities and stage-specific quantities, and the quantitative fulfillment relation remain unclosed. R001 and R004 respectively share only the internal balance and collective wholesale access interfaces.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The basis for assembly is the continuing effect of day-ahead decisions across scenarios, intraday remediation, and their dependence as they enter the same expected net-cost objective, rather than a common coordinator or process sequence. The cost components of R010 are used to explain the R008 objective and do not add another cost. Participation and product rules and local price selection each retain independent boundaries.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Defines the responsibility boundary under which STEP coordinates automatically according to community rules and does not acquire electricity ownership, and provides the community cost-minimization purpose."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the inputs, surplus condition, and commitment obligation for the day-ahead joint supply bid."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the household-by-household two-stage allocation, scenario supply-demand constraints, energy storage limits, and expected net-cost objective."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides trading execution permission, fulfillment of day-ahead commitments, external purchase and sale directions, and conditional intraday supplementary purchase; its P2P balance is associated in K001 as an alternative expression."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Provides the electricity purchase cost, feed-in compensation, and objective-component accounting for the same external transaction quantity, without extending to a complete household-by-household internal settlement system."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Shares only the community P2P aggregate balance and related quantity interfaces; the specific bridge to stage-specific quantities remains listed as a gap."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cites only the community collective wholesale participation permission of C002 and does not turn that permission into a mandatory bid or quantity constraint."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07"],"rationale":"The collective wholesale participation permission and the specific day-ahead bidding activity are complementary; the participation permission itself does not mean that a supply bid must be submitted in all circumstances."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e08"],"rationale":"The same source explicitly assigns automatic bidding based on community information to STEP and limits it to a computational interface that does not hold electricity; this is a correspondence between responsibility and activity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e30"],"rationale":"STEP's community expected cost objective is concretely carried by the resource allocation optimization of the same framework; other independent constraints are not merged because of the common agent."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::x::x_F_DA"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04"],"rationale":"Day-ahead bidding and allocation are both based on forecasts and must consider supply-demand security in each scenario. Here only the planning and fulfillment functions are associated, and F_DA is not identified as a bid quantity that has not yet been declared."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"],"rationale":"The two records come from the same statement on fulfillment of day-ahead commitments and appear respectively as a bidding-side obligation and an execution-side logical relation; the alternative expressions are retained and not counted as an additional obligation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::x::x_G_ID"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"Intraday electricity purchase is a supply-demand remediation option described by the source and appears on the second-stage supply side; this correspondence does not prove that the optimization has strictly implemented the trigger conditions of using P2P and energy storage first."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C009"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_F_DA","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E02"],"rationale":"The day-ahead feed-in permission, the intraday export prohibition, and the feed-in source restriction define the trading scope of the allocation model; the existing quantity definitions are not yet sufficient to prove that the source restriction has been implemented mathematically."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-I","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_X_DA","v141-c-R008::x::x_X_ID","v141-c-R008::x::x_I_DA","v141-c-R008::x::x_I_ID"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The aggregate balance and stage-specific allocation involve the same community P2P activity and constitute a quantity interface to be closed; the source does not specify the bridge, and the aggregate quantity cannot be directly equated with the sum of DA and ID quantities."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L09","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_G_DA","v141-c-R008::x::x_F_DA","v141-c-R008::x::x_G_ID"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x001","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x002","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"On the allocation side, day-ahead electricity purchase, day-ahead feed-in, and intraday electricity purchase are respectively the same model transaction quantities used in cost accounting, while their local functional roles remain separate."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L10","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"R010 records the day-ahead and expected intraday cost components of the same objective, and R008 is responsible for minimizing their total; the overall optimization and component accounting are not duplicate complete expressions and cannot be charged twice."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L11","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"shared_node","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"Both chains reference the same execution function, and the source attaches the external electricity purchase cost and day-ahead feed-in compensation to the corresponding transactions; this does not turn all P2P execution content into external payment obligations."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e08"],"rationale":"Four frozen nodes reference the same STEP computational interface; only the reference containing the role description is selected for node display, while all original bidding, allocation, and execution bindings are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"Both are the same frozen clearing node; only the node display is unified, and the community P2P aggregate balance and household-by-household supply-demand constraint are not treated as duplicate rules."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g03-E03"],"rationale":"The same day-ahead supply bidding function appears respectively in the submission and fulfillment relations; only the node reference display is unified, and its conditions or edges are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"The payment chain and the execution chain use the same frozen execution node; the display representative does not change the execution conditions or the scope of application of the payment edge."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_G_DA","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"],"rationale":"Both are the household-by-household, hour-by-hour day-ahead grid electricity purchase quantity of the same model, used respectively for allocation and cost accounting; the local variables remain separate."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_F_DA","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"],"rationale":"Both are the same household-by-household, hour-by-hour day-ahead feed-in quantity, entering resource allocation and compensation accounting respectively; no bid-quantity identity is constructed on this basis."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_G_ID","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"Both are the intraday electricity purchase quantity for the same time step, household, and scenario, assuming different local roles of supply-demand remediation and expected cost accounting."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_p_G_DA","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31"],"rationale":"Both record the same parameter used in Eq. (15) for pricing day-ahead electricity purchase; the original notation descriptions in Table 1 and the equation are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_p_F","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e36"],"rationale":"Both record the same day-ahead feed-in compensation price, serving optimization and accounting respectively; the original parameter records are not rewritten."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_p_G_ID","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"Both are the intraday grid electricity purchase price for the same time step and scenario in Eq. (16), with consistent semantics and applicable stage, while the local records remain separate."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_pi","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e32"],"rationale":"Both records refer to the scenario probability weight in Eq. (16); based on the probability meaning and the association in the same equation, the notation difference between π_s and π^(s) is retained, and no additional scenario-construction assumption is introduced."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M12","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"],"rationale":"The same source obligation forms a bidding-side statement and an execution-side logical constraint respectively; the expression types and bindings differ, and they are associated as alternative expressions and all retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All assembly links are still supported only by unaudited evidence permitted by the experiment; the B transcription, existing C content, and this cluster have not received independent scientific confirmation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32","v141-b-g02-e38","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Retain the candidate and unaudited status; if scientific confirmation is subsequently required, independent source checking and cluster-by-cluster manual inspection should be arranged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The existing C does not retain the complete counterparty flow structure of Eqs. (6) to (8), nor does it clarify the relationship between aggregate P2P quantities and DA and ID quantities, and it cannot be claimed that Eq. (9) has closed the allocation across stages.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-I","v141-c-R008::x::x_X_DA","v141-c-R008::x::x_X_ID","v141-c-R008::x::x_I_DA","v141-c-R008::x::x_I_ID","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C011"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should verify the stage indices and quantity definitions and supplement the source-supported flow and stage interfaces; D must not independently determine that the aggregate quantity equals the sum of DA and ID."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The statement that a joint bid may be chosen when forecast renewable generation exceeds demand is not clearly consistent, in trigger timing and obligation strength, with the source statement that a commitment is made when production exceeds demand.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g03-E03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the case and forecast scope of the two statements and distinguish between bidding choice and post-commitment fulfillment obligations; before clarification, do not rewrite them into a unified mandatory submission rule."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R007 does not declare a bid quantity, and the R009 fulfillment obligation is not formalized; the existing chain does not connect the committed quantity with F_DA and the actual delivered quantities in each scenario. Household-by-household supply-demand security does not automatically prove committed delivery.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R008::x::x_F_DA","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check how the source represents commitment, feed-in, and delivery, and have C supplement a supported quantity interface or clarify that it is only a procedural obligation; D does not add fulfillment formulas."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Whether the stage-specific quantities are incremental or independent non-negative quantities, and the bounds and units of the transaction quantities, are not specified; the energy storage recursion includes the first time point but the previous-period state is undefined, and the compatibility between the zero initial state and the lower bound is not given. The dimensional relationship between the half-hour time step and the charge/discharge rate still needs verification.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::x::x_S","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_alpha","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_beta","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x001","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x002","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g02-e29","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Recheck the variable domains, the meaning of stage increments, the first-step state boundary, and the power and energy units, and check feasibility and objective boundedness; do not independently infer the non-negativity of each component from the two-stage aggregate bounds."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G06","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The scenario-disabling conditions, feed-in source restrictions, and conditional intraday supplementary purchase of R009 do not yet have complete interfaces entering the R008 feasible region. An intraday export variable aligned with the prohibition direction does not appear, but this is insufficient to prove that all trading restrictions have been implemented.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C009","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e38"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check how the case switches, feed-in source tracking, and intraday purchase trigger are implemented in the source model; have C supplement or clarify the procedural applicability conditions, and do not add narrative order as a priority constraint."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G07","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R008 retains the source assertion that internal P2P costs offset at the community level, but the loss balance makes the total sold and purchased quantities differ; the existing chain does not explain the measurement basis for internal receipts and payments or the bearing of loss costs, and monetary offset cannot be derived from the existing quantity relations. R010 provides only external transaction accounting.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C012","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify whether the offset in the community objective is a modeling assumption or is supported by an independent internal accounting rule, and check loss allocation; do not invent household-by-household P2P payment formulas or modify the existing objective."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G08","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The physical limits of energy storage are currently carried by clearing.local, and there is no approved independent energy storage resource or operation node. Both related node proposals remain pending, and energy storage functions cannot be considered independently modeled on this basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::x::x_S"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g02-e29"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-prop-01","v141-b-g04-p01"],"required_work":"Manually inspect the operation and resource boundaries of the two proposals; if an extension is approved, first update the framework and C bindings. This round retains the original clearing attribution and does not insert nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G09","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The source lists smart grid, complete information exchange, and the price-taker assumption as framework assumptions, but the current chain does not fully express these applicability conditions, and they cannot be directly generalized to strategic games or markets with incomplete information.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g04-e08","v141-b-g04-e09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should supplement source-grounded applicability-scope records, and manually confirm the limits these assumptions place on automatic coordination and optimization interpretation; D does not add scientific objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G10","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R008-C004 exists in the frozen chain but is not included in the given current_C2_bindings; the existing binding records for this first-stage expected scenario condition are incomplete.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should supplement or explain the binding of this constraint to existing nodes; D only records the omission, does not rewrite the frozen C content, and is not regarded as having completed an independent C2 review."}]},"rule_refs":["32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R002","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R007","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R008","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R009","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R010","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R001","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-374de966ac2aa057","COMP-38f1b9199b3ea8cd","COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-8194bc76303bef38","COMP-970463b73869ba14","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9"]});
